</span>.<span class=\"name\">VCGen</span>.<span class=\"name\">State</span>.<span class=\"name\">specBackwardRuleCache</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">self</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/VCGen/Context.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.VCGen.State\">State</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Data/HashMap/Basic.html#Std.HashMap\">Std.HashMap</a> (<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/ExprPtr.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.ExprPtr\">Meta.Sym.ExprPtr</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>) <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/Apply.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.BackwardRule\">Meta.Sym.BackwardRule</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"A cache mapping registered SpecThms to their backward rule to apply.\nThe particular rule depends on the theorem name, the `WPMonad` instance and the number of\nexcess state arguments that the weakest precondition target is applied to.\n\nThe instance is keyed by `ExprPtr`, so lookups compare it by pointer rather than structurally.\nThis is sound because the instance is a subterm of the hash-consed goal target.","docLink":"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/VCGen/Context.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.VCGen.State.specBackwardRuleCache","kind":"def","line":187,"name":"Lean.Elab.Tactic.VCGen.State.specBackwardRuleCache","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Elab/Tactic/VCGen/Context.lean#L187-L187"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">constructor</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Elab/Tactic/VCGen/Context.html#Lean.Elab.Tactic.VCGen.State.mk\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Elab</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">VCGen</span>.<span class=\"name\">State</span>.<spa